{{Quote|Master Windu, you have fought gallantly&hellip;worthy of recognition in the archives of the Jedi Order. Now it is finished. Surrender, and your lives will be spared."''<br />''"We will not be hostages to be bartered, Dooku."''<br />''"Then, I'm sorry, old friend.|Dooku offers Gon and the other Jedi a chance to surrender, which is refused by Mace Windu|audio=DookuAndWindu-Surrender.flac|<ref name="AOTC" />}}
'''Tarados Gon''' was a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Klatooinian]] who served as a [[Jedi Knight]] in the [[Jedi Order]]. In [[22 BBY]], Gon was part of the [[Jedi assault team|assault team]] led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Mace Windu]] that traveled to the [[planet]] [[Geonosis]] to save [[Jedi]] Knight [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] from [[Death|execution]] by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].

The Jedi [[First Battle of Geonosis|engaged]] the [[Separatist Droid Army|Separatist forces]] in the [[Petranaki Arena]] but sustained heavy casualties, with Gon and the other survivors eventually finding themselves surrounded. After refusing to surrender to the Separatist [[Count of Serenno|Count]] [[Dooku]], the Jedi were rescued by the arrival of an [[Grand Army of the Republic|army]] of [[clone trooper]]s led by [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]], which turned the battle around and defeated the Separatists.

==Biography==
===Geonosis strike team===
{{Quote|I will take what Jedi we have left and go to Geonosis and help Obi-Wan.|Mace Windu|audio=Windu-WhatJedi.flac|<ref name="AOTC" />}}
[[File:Geonosis_arena.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Tarados Gon fought in the Geonosis arena.]]
Tarados Gon was a [[Klatooinian]] member of the [[Jedi Order]] who served as a guardian of the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="Species Guide" /> By the [[Standard year|year]] [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]'' dates the events of {{Film|II}} to [[22 BBY]].</ref> Gon had risen to the rank of [[Jedi Knight]]<ref name="Species Guide" /> and was part of an [[Jedi assault team|assault team]]<ref name="AOTC" /> made up of 212 [[Jedi]]<ref name="UVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> led by [[Jedi Master]] [[Mace Windu]] that traveled to the [[planet]] [[Geonosis]] in order to rescue Jedi Knight [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]].<ref name="AOTC" />

Kenobi had been captured by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], a group of [[Politics|political]] entities and companies seeking to [[Separatist Crisis|separate]] from the Republic. He was due to be [[Death|executed]] in the [[Geonosian]] [[Petranaki Arena]] alongside his [[Padawan]], [[Anakin Skywalker]], and [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]], both of whom had been captured trying to rescue Kenobi.<ref name="AOTC" />

===The Battle of Geonosis===
{{Quote|However, not all Klatooinians are drawn to the underworld. Some have been known to be Force-sensitive, and there were some Klatooinian Jedi Knights, such as Tarados Gon, that fought in the Battle of Geonosis.|An entry in an artist's journal restored and expanded at the Graf Archive|<ref name="Species Guide" />}}
[[File:JediCircle.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Tarados Gon (far right) was amongst the final surviving Jedi in the arena on Geonosis.]]
Gon and the other Jedi infiltrated the arena while the three [[prisoner]]s fought to avoid death. The group of Jedi revealed themselves when Windu confronted [[Head of State|Separatist leader]] [[Count of Serenno|Count]] [[Dooku]]. The Jedi then [[First Battle of Geonosis|engaged]] an [[Separatist Droid Army|army]] of [[battle droid]]s deployed to the arena, with Gon fighting on the arena floor.<ref name="AOTC" />

The Jedi sustained heavy casualties, and soon Gon and most of the other survivors found themselves surrounded in a circle at the center of the arena. Dooku called for his [[droid]]s to cease firing and commended the efforts of the Jedi, before offering them a chance to surrender.<ref name="AOTC" />

===Last stand===
{{Quote|Around the survivors a perimeter create.|Yoda orders his troops to protect Tarados Gon and the other Jedi|audio=Yoda-Perimeter.flac|<ref name="AOTC" />}}
[[File:Laatis_arrive_on_Geonosis.png|thumb|left|250px|The arrival of the clone army saved the Jedi on Geonosis.]]
Windu refused the offer, and Dooku gave the order for Gon and the others to be killed. However, before the battle droids could begin firing, [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry]] [[gunship]]s descended on the arena carrying an [[Grand Army of the Republic|army]] of [[clone trooper]]s led by Jedi [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]].<ref name="AOTC" />

As the droids began firing, the gunships landed in a perimeter around the surviving Jedi in order to rescue them. The Jedi then boarded the [[Starship|ships]], which left the arena and carried their occupants to join the wider battle outside. The arrival of the clones ultimately turned the battle in the Jedi and Republic's favor, allowing them to defeat the Separatist forces and force them to flee Geonosis. The battle marked the start of<ref name="AOTC" /> [[the galaxy]]-wide<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="AOTC" />

===Legacy===
In the year [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> the aspiring Jedi [[Luke Skywalker]] [[Duel on Cloud City|engaged]] the [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth]] Vader, the [[Sith]] identity of Anakin Skywalker, in [[Cloud City]] on the planet [[Bespin]]. During the [[lightsaber duel]], Skywalker used a [[Force jump]] to escape a [[carbon-freezing chamber]] laid out as a trap by Vader. His jump was as high and quick as those once performed by Gon.<ref name="Odyssey">''[[The Odyssey of Star Wars: An Epic Poem]]''</ref> Gon was mentioned in an [[Unidentified artist|artist's]] [[Unidentified artist's journal|journal]], which was restored, expanded, and displayed at the [[Graf Archive]]<ref name="Alien Archives">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> at some point no earlier than [[34 ABY]].<ref name="Year">{{AlienArchiveJournalDate}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
Tarados Gon was a [[Force-sensitive]] Klatooinian<ref name="Species Guide" /> with [[Color|brown]] skin.<ref name="AOTC" />

==Powers and abilities==
Gon was a noted and skilled user of the Force jump [[Force power|power]], which he could perform with speed and to achieve great heights.<ref name="Odyssey" />

==Equipment==
Gon wore a light-brown [[Jedi apparel|tunic]] with dark-brown pants and used a blue-bladed [[lightsaber]].<ref name="AOTC" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:TiinGonHandshake-SkywalkerSaga.png|thumb|right|200px|Tarados Gon and Saesee Tiin shake hands in a deleted scene.]]
Tarados Gon first appeared in the [[2002]] [[prequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']], played by an uncredited actor.<ref name="AOTC" /> The character was first identified by name in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the [[2018]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]'', written by [[Natalie Clubb]] and [[Katrina Pallant]].<ref name="Species Guide" />

The Jedi battle in the Geonosis Arena scenes were filmed on Stage 3 at [[Fox Studios, Sydney]], between [[August 10]] and [[August 15]], [[2000]].<ref name="Archives">''[[The Star Wars Archives: Episodes I–III, 1999–2005]]''</ref> In an unused and unfinished alternate cut of the Battle of Geonosis in which a group of Jedi board a [[Lucrehulk-class battleship|Droid Control Ship]] during the arena battle, Tarados Gon can be seen shaking hands with [[Saesee Tiin]] in the circle of surviving Jedi after they seemingly manage to shut down the droids attacking them. The droids then reactivate, leaving the Jedi surrounded once more.<ref name="Complete Saga">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Star Wars: The Skywalker Saga|scene=Raid on the Droid Control Ship}}</ref>

Although Gon's lightsaber is primarily shown as blue in color throughout ''Attack of the Clones'', it is erroneously green in color during the shot in which Mace Windu refuses to surrender to Count Dooku, and another brief shot when the [[Low Altitude Assault Transport]]s land to rescue the Jedi strike team.<ref name="AOTC" /> The character's name originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first used in the [[2003]] reference book ''[[Inside the Worlds of Star Wars: Attack of the Clones]]'', written by [[Curtis Saxton]] and [[Simon Beecroft]].<ref name="Inside AOTC">''[[Inside the Worlds of Star Wars: Attack of the Clones]]''</ref>

